IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- EVIDENCE OF AGE AND IDENTITY (regulations 47 to 51).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 482 to 499.
--
-- How the Minister determines a person's age and identity for the Act: first a birth certificate (or a copy, or a copy
-- of an act of birth) or the information the Canada Employment Insurance Commission makes available (47(1)); the
-- Minister may ask for the original where the copy is doubtful (47(2)), may fall back on other information where the
-- documents are not available (47(3)), and then on Statistics Canada (47(4)); may accept an age settled under the Old
-- Age Security Act or a provincial pension plan (49); may redetermine on new facts (50). Regulation 51 sets the
-- conditions of a request to Statistics Canada and who may see what it returns.
-- Each "may" here is a power of the Minister, which is the person's liability; each is a BOOLEAN saying the power exists.

§ `Part V -- Evidence of age and identity (regulations 47 to 51)`

§§ `Regulation 47 -- how the Minister determines age and identity`

-- src:483 | 47 (1) Subject to subsections (2) to (4) and sections 49 and 50, the Minister must determine a person’s age and identity for the purposes of the Act on the basis of
-- src:484 | (a) a birth certificate, a copy of one or a copy of an act of birth, or
-- src:485 | (b) any information made available to the Minister by the Canada Employment Insurance Commission under subsection 28.2(5) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
@ref Reg 47(1) (src:483-485)
GIVEN `a birth certificate, a copy of one or a copy of an act of birth is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information is made available to the Minister by the Canada Employment Insurance Commission under subsection 28.2(5) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 47(1) — the Minister must determine the person's age and identity on the basis of a document or information in subsection (1)`
    `a birth certificate, a copy of one or a copy of an act of birth is available`
    `information is made available to the Minister by the Canada Employment Insurance Commission under subsection 28.2(5) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` MEANS
    `a birth certificate, a copy of one or a copy of an act of birth is available`
        OR `information is made available to the Minister by the Canada Employment Insurance Commission under subsection 28.2(5) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`

-- src:486 | (2) If there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a birth certificate or act of birth referred to in paragraph (1)(a), the Minister may require that the original birth certificate or, if applicable, a copy of the act of birth issued by the competent authority be furnished.
@ref Reg 47(2) (src:486)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a birth certificate or act of birth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 47(2) — the Minister may require the original birth certificate or a copy of the act of birth issued by the competent authority`
    `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a birth certificate or act of birth` MEANS
    `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a birth certificate or act of birth`

-- src:487 | (3) If there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available, the Minister may determine the person’s age and identity on the basis of any other information or evidence respecting the person’s age and identity.
@ref Reg 47(3) (src:487)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 47(3) — the Minister may determine the person's age and identity on the basis of any other information or evidence`
    `there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available` MEANS
    `there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available`

-- src:488 | (4) If the Minister is unable to determine the person’s age and identity under any of subsections (1) to (3), the Minister may, if possible, determine them on the basis of any information obtained from Statistics Canada under section 87 of the Act.
@ref Reg 47(4) (src:488)
GIVEN `the Minister is unable to determine the person's age and identity under any of subsections (1) to (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is possible to determine them on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada under section 87 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 47(4) — the Minister may determine the person's age and identity on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada`
    `the Minister is unable to determine the person's age and identity under any of subsections (1) to (3)`
    `it is possible to determine them on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada under section 87 of the Act` MEANS
    `the Minister is unable to determine the person's age and identity under any of subsections (1) to (3)`
        AND `it is possible to determine them on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada under section 87 of the Act`

§§ `Regulations 49 and 50 -- accepting and redetermining an age`

-- src:490 | 49 If a person’s age has been determined under the Old Age Security Act or a provincial pension plan, the Minister may accept that determination for the purposes of the Act.
@ref Reg 49 (src:490)
GIVEN `the person's age has been determined under the Old Age Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's age has been determined under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 49 — the Minister may accept the determination of the person's age for the purposes of the Act`
    `the person's age has been determined under the Old Age Security Act`
    `the person's age has been determined under a provincial pension plan` MEANS
    `the person's age has been determined under the Old Age Security Act`
        OR `the person's age has been determined under a provincial pension plan`

-- src:491 | 50 At any time after the age of a person has been determined pursuant to these Regulations, the Minister may, where facts not previously taken into account in determining the age of the person come to his attention, make a new determination of the age of the person.
@ref Reg 50 (src:491)
GIVEN `the age of the person has been determined pursuant to these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `facts not previously taken into account in determining the age have come to the Minister's attention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 50 — the Minister may make a new determination of the age of the person`
    `the age of the person has been determined pursuant to these Regulations`
    `facts not previously taken into account in determining the age have come to the Minister's attention` MEANS
    `the age of the person has been determined pursuant to these Regulations`
        AND `facts not previously taken into account in determining the age have come to the Minister's attention`

§§ `Regulation 51 -- requests to Statistics Canada, and who may see the answer`

-- src:492 | 51 For the purposes of section 87 of the Act, the following are prescribed as the conditions subject to which any information specified in that section respecting the age of any applicant or beneficiary or the applicant’s or beneficiary’s spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner is obtainable from Statistics Canada on request and for the purpose specified in that section:
-- src:493 | (a) the request to Statistics Canada must
-- src:494 | (i) be made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician,
-- src:495 | (ii) bear the signed consent of the applicant, beneficiary, spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner or of the person or agency that made the application on their behalf or, where there is no such person or agency, any other person or agency who would have been entitled to make the application on their behalf, and
-- src:496 | (iii) provide such information as may be necessary to enable a proper search to be made of the census records for the purpose of obtaining the information requested; and
-- src:497 | (b) information obtained under section 87 of the Act must not be disclosed to any person other than an officer, clerk or employee of the Department of Employment and Social Development or other than as required by an agreement entered into under section 105 of the Act.
@ref Reg 51(a) (src:492-496)
GIVEN `the request is made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request bears the signed consent of the person, or of the person or agency that made the application for them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request provides the information necessary for a proper search of the census records` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 51(a) — a request to Statistics Canada meets the prescribed conditions`
    `the request is made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician`
    `the request bears the signed consent of the person, or of the person or agency that made the application for them`
    `the request provides the information necessary for a proper search of the census records` MEANS
    `the request is made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician`
        AND `the request bears the signed consent of the person, or of the person or agency that made the application for them`
        AND `the request provides the information necessary for a proper search of the census records`

-- "Of the person": the applicant, beneficiary, spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner whose
-- age the request is about; where nobody made the application for them, any other person or agency entitled to make it.
@ref Reg 51(b) (src:497)
GIVEN `the recipient is an officer, clerk or employee of the Department of Employment and Social Development` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is required by an agreement entered into under section 105 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 105 (piece cp6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 51(b) — information obtained from Statistics Canada may be disclosed to a person`
    `the recipient is an officer, clerk or employee of the Department of Employment and Social Development`
    `the disclosure is required by an agreement entered into under section 105 of the Act` MEANS
    `the recipient is an officer, clerk or employee of the Department of Employment and Social Development`
        OR `the disclosure is required by an agreement entered into under section 105 of the Act`
